                <pb facs="0870" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg784"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to the
                            Sublime Porte.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November 13,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I hasten to return the notice
                    which the Sublime Porte addressed to the legation late last evening in reference
                    to the attempt made against the life of the American vice-consul at Beirut.</p>
                <p>This notice must have been forwarded in error as the circumstances demand a
                    different reply, both in form and contents.</p>
                <p>I take this occasion, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John G. A.
                    Leishman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
